A||N||2||Bob Englert||EGR tube replacement ?||||1||
Z||000000||Bob Englert||12-20-2000||10:42 PM||||While replaced a worn out EGR valve on my 87 GT 5 sp I broke the EGR tube near the EGR valve.  I have a new tube on order, but I was wondering if anyone could briefly list the sequence of removal steps required to replace this.  I have never removed the plenum on the car.  Any guidance or references to a good manual would be appreciated.<P>Also, where can I get the EGR tube gaskets?  They do not appear to be available from GM anymore.<P>Thanks...<P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000001||2xsess||12-20-2000||11:22 PM||||I think Ed Parks told me that almost any parts store should be able to get the gaskets. He said that they usually don't go bad and can be reused. <P>When I replaced my EGR tube I didn't remove anything but the EGR valve and the little block thingy it sits on, oh and also the coil. The dang heatshield was in the way.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Predator||12-21-2000||07:19 AM||||I broke mine as well a while back. They are prone to cracking because they are not very flexable. I got a new tube from Kevin at Design One Systems. It is better because it is flexable and will not break over time. He also furnished new gaskets with it. All you should have to do is take the distributer cap off to be able to get to where it connects under the intake manifold. Then use a 10m wrench to unbolt it and it should just come off. Then replace it by installing the manifold end first. Be sure not to overtighten the bolts. I am not sure what the turque rating is, but just make them good and snug.The bad thing about the GM replacement is it will eventually break or crack again. It will last for years though. I am not trying to make the GM replacement sound bad. It took me about 30 minutes for the whole procedure. It is a pain getting to the bolts under the manifold, but it will work. ||||reg||1
